{"Title":"An Act relative to a charitable tax credit","BillNumber":"H2925","DocketNumber":"HD336","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"AJP1","Name":"Angelo J. Puppolo, Jr.","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/AJP1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-10T13:54:28.533"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"AJP1","Name":"Angelo J. Puppolo, Jr.","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/AJP1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-10T13:54:28.5333333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H2925/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Puppolo of Springfield, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 2925) of Angelo J. Puppolo, Jr. relative to providing for a charitable tax credit.  Revenue.","DocumentText":"\tChapter 62 of the General Laws is hereby amended by inserting after section 6N the following section:-\r\n\tSection 6O. There shall be a credit against the taxes imposed by this chapter equal to the amount donated by an individual to public charities within the commonwealth. In the case of a single person or a married person filing a separate return or a head of household, the total credit shall not exceed $300. In the case of a married couple filing a joint return, the total credit shall not exceed $300 for each individual.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J26","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J26"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}